{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>In their land you shall not inherit, etc.</b> In Sifrei they said that He forbade to him a portion of the land and a portion of the spoil, and therefore He repeated to say <b>you shall not inherit and a portion you shall not have</b>, etc. And the intent of the verse is that even if Israel wished to apportion him a share with them, one should not say that HaShem intended only to exempt Israel from Aaron's portion — rather, if they wish to, these are praiseworthy, along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Shevi'it 10:9): one who repays a debt in the Sabbatical year — the spirit of the Sages is pleased with him. Therefore He said <b>you shall not inherit</b> — and I would understand that it is specifically the inheritance of the land that is under prohibition, but the portion of the spoil is not prohibited; Scripture comes to teach <b>and a portion</b>, etc. And note carefully that He said <b>in their midst</b>, along the lines of the verse (Proverbs 1:14): ״גּוֹרָלְךָ תַּפִּיל בְּתוֹכֵנוּ״ — meaning, to take a portion as one of them, that is what He forbade to him; but if they wished to send him gifts, he may receive them from them." "<b>I am your portion, etc., in the midst of the children of Israel.</b> The verse's saying <b>I</b> — meaning: that which is uniquely designated for Me, I shall be your portion. And He went back and explained what that thing is, and said <b>in the midst of</b>, etc. — that there is nothing that Israel do in which the Holy One, blessed be He, does not have a portion with them, and the priest takes it: in the produce of the land, in the fruit of the tree, in bread, in meat, in wine, in oil, and the rest of the twenty-four gifts."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:57.210694934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}